# Each word sells a feature instead of describing it. `first class`
# and `super` are left out, because each names something in code (a
# first-class function, a superclass call). `enduring` stays out too
# (`enduring storage outlives the pod`).
#
# `robust` keeps a technical sense behind a guard, since `robust to`
# names a statistical property (`robust to outliers`). A negated word
# after a space needs a word to consume, so `robust` has a twin for a
# clause end (`robust!( )`). `highly` sits in the intensifier rule,
# because it raises an adjective rather than selling a feature.
#
# A space in a pattern matches only whitespace, so each compound that
# writers also hyphenate takes `[-, ( )]` between its words and
# matches `battle tested` and `battle-tested` alike.
expr main [seamless, seamlessly, (robust !to), (robust!( )), powerful, elegant, elegantly, comprehensive, intuitive, effortless, effortlessly, blazing, blazingly, revolutionary, innovative, sophisticated, intricate, vibrant, (a breeze), holistic, groundbreaking, transformative, (ever[-, ( )]evolving), (rapidly evolving), (top[-, ( )]notch), (battle[-, ( )]tested), (production[-, ( )]ready), (enterprise[-, ( )]grade), (out[-, ( )]of[-, ( )]the[-, ( )]box), (bells and whistles), (feature[-, ( )]rich), (cutting[-, ( )]edge), (state[-, ( )]of[-, ( )]the[-, ( )]art), (lightning[-, ( )]fast), (best[-, ( )]in[-, ( )]class), (world[-, ( )]class), (next[-, ( )]generation), (game[-, ( )]changing), (game[-, ( )]changer), (game[-, ( )]changers)]
let message "Marketing language. State the fact and let the reader judge its weight."
let description "Flags marketing adjectives that inflate a claim without informing."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The bucket refills every second."
allows "The estimator is robust to outliers."
allows "Go has first-class functions."
